.TH deroff "" "Command"
.SH NAME
deroff \- remove text formatting control information
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBderoff [\-s] [\-w] [\-x] [\fIfile ...\fB]\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.HS
deroff -- remove text formatting control information
Usage:	deroff [ -w ] [ -x ] [ file ... ]
Options:
	-w	Divide the output into words, one per line
	-x	Extra knowledge of macro packages (knows about .NH, .DS, etc.)
Removes nroff control information from each 'file', or standard input if none.
.HE
.B deroff
strips
.B nroff
and
.B troff
formatting control information from each
.IR file ,
or from the standard input if no
.I file
is given, and writes what remains to the standard output.
Any line beginning with a period or an apostrophe is taken to be a
formatting request and is discarded, except that:
.IP \- 0.3i
text between \fB.EQ\fR and \fB.EN\fR (eqn), and between \fB.TS\fR and
\fB.TE\fR (tbl), is discarded entirely, as are macro definitions
(from \fB.de\fR up to the closing \fB..\fR line);
.IP \-
.B .so
and
.B .nx
requests cause the named file to be read in place of the request,
and no file is read more than once;
.IP \-
backslash escapes such as font and point-size changes, and interpolated
strings, registers, and characters, are stripped from the surviving
text, along with anything between a leading eqn delimiter character
and its matching trailing delimiter (as most recently set by a
.B delim
line inside an
.B .EQ
block).
.IP \-s
Accepted on the command line but has no effect in this version.
.IP \-w
Instead of copying ordinary text through unchanged, break it into
words and print one per line.
A word is a maximal run of letters, digits, and apostrophes that
begins with a letter; apostrophes are stripped from the printed word,
and everything else between words is discarded.
.IP \-x
Use additional knowledge of the
.B \-ms
macro package: discard footnotes (between \fB.FS\fR and \fB.FE\fR),
no-fill displays (between \fB.nf\fR and \fB.fi\fR), and displays
(between \fB.DS\fR or \fB.KS\fR/\fB.KF\fR and \fB.DE\fR or \fB.KE\fR);
also skip title and author lines (\fB.TL\fR, \fB.AI\fR, \fB.AU\fR,
\fB.SH\fR, \fB.NH\fR) up to the next control line.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.B nroff
.SH NOTES
The word-division mode (\fB\-w\fR) is intended for the
spelling-checker pipeline; it is not itself a spelling checker.
.PP
The
.B \-s
option is accepted for compatibility but currently does nothing; only
.B \-w
and
.B \-x
change
.BR deroff 's
behavior.
